{
  "name": "Sanaku - T1 Reply Handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## T1 - Reply Handler\n\nThe customer texts back after the missed-call auto-reply. This decides whether they are a real lead and gets the owner involved fast.\n\n1. **STOP first, always.** Any opt-out wording -> permanent per-client suppression, a courtesy confirmation, and nothing else ever again. This runs before any qualification.\n2. Match the inbound number to the open lead for that client.\n3. Qualify against the client's OWN `qualified_definition` (the wording that is in their signed agreement) via OpenRouter, with a keyword fallback so a model outage never drops a lead.\n4. Update the lead: `qualified`, `lead_score`, `outcome`, and the conversation transcript. **`qualified` is what gets billed**, so this is the meter.\n5. Alert the client's escalation contact immediately on a qualified or urgent lead - speed is the entire product.\n\nSet your provider's inbound-SMS webhook to POST here.\n\nCredentials: \"Supabase Service Role (Custom Auth)\", \"Twilio account\", \"OpenRouter (Header Auth)\".\nEnv: SUPABASE_URL, optional OPENROUTER_MODEL.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 540
      },
      "id": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000099",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        40,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "t1-reply",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
